From 96299c93a166b468a9586fc3a039ff7d4a256426 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 12:06:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add model execution, inference engine, and benchmarking
 framework

Phase 1: Live inference platform
- New models: ResearcherProfile, MLModel, InferenceRun with full medical
  imaging metadata (modality, body region, architecture choices, etc.)
- PyTorch inference engine with model loading, preprocessing (JPEG/PNG/
  DICOM/NIfTI), softmax classification, and LRU model cache
- GradCAM explainability with auto-detected target layers per architecture
- Model upload with server-side validation (loads model + runs dummy pass)
- HTMX-powered "Try It" inference UI with drag-and-drop, demo button,
  probability bars, and GradCAM overlay display
- Rate limiting (20 runs/IP/hour), research-use disclaimers
- Auth: login, register with ResearcherProfile, approval gating

Phase 2: Benchmarking framework
- New models: Benchmark, BenchmarkEntry with flexible JSON metrics
- Sortable comparison tables, pipeline detail accordions
- Side-by-side model comparison view
- Integration: models link to benchmarks they appear in

Seed data: 3 real PyTorch models (ResNet18, DenseNet121, EfficientNet-B0)
with random weights, demo images, and 2 benchmarks with 7 entries total.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M5TpWhJvmqo5SMubVpxoqF
